! mcp_bootstrap_p188.strap -- MCP printed page 188: the I/O INDICATOR
! CHECK routine, K IO IND, complete from its banner to its last card.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.195.  The header was READ, not
! assumed, at 400 dpi:  "TIME CLOCK 00054041   PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID LG000001   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  188".
!
! >>> THE COLUMN-HEADING ROW'S OWN "LOCATION" FIELD IS BLANK. <<<
! Rendered at 600 dpi over the whole span between the word LOCATION
! and the right margin: dashed rule and nothing else.  That is the
! workflow's rule behaving: the field is LINE 1's location and line 1
! here is an asterisk banner that compiles nothing.  A blank is NOT a
! zero and no digits were invented from the rule.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FORTY-SEVEN PRINTED LINES, card serials LG000001..LG000040 with no
! gap, then blank paper to the foot of the form.  Lines 1-3 are the
! asterisk banner, 5-7 comment cards, line 4 a printed "SLC,$".  The
! forty located rows run 221370.00 .. 221415.00 CONTIGUOUSLY -- every
! one a half word, no DR, no DRZ, no forward SLC, NO HOLE.
!
!   lines  8-18   K IO IND: test the EPGK and UK indicators, return
!                 at once if neither is on, else save the IC in
!                 K K IND and sort the failure by its operation --
!                 space file, write label, read label, write tape
!                 mark -- into the four KVI/BXE pairs.
!   lines 19-31   K REPET, the locate/change-density arm: reissue the
!                 command as a SEOP, retry through K IO REJ, then
!                 check termination at J SEOP T and dispatch on
!                 EPGK / UK / EE / success.  K COUNT counts the
!                 retries with a CB against K REPET.
!   lines 32-47   K R READ, the read-label arm: backspace over the
!                 label (J BSP X / J BSP E), K R NEW reissues the read
!                 from the index word R RDL, and K R UK counts its
!                 retries with a CB against K R READ.
!
! THE TYPESET MANUAL DESCRIBES THIS EXACT PAGE, which is a second
! reading of nearly every name on it.  C22-6728 Service Routines
! printed p.183:
!
!   "After a non-SEOP set up I-O operation, the I-O indicator check
!    routine (KIOIND, Figure 107) is used to test the EPGK and UK
!    indicators. ... The five main paths through the routine are:
!      1. KKSPAC  Space file failure
!      2. KLABWL  Write label failure
!      3. KRREAD  Read label failure
!      4. KRWEF   Write tape mark failure
!      5. KREPET  Locate or change density failure"
!
! and, on the page before, the calling sequence itself:
!
!      "SIC, KKIND
!       B, KIOIND"
!
! which is word for word this page's line 6 comment card.  Five of
! those six names are what the ink reads.  The sixth, "KLABWL", is
! the PROSE's name for path 2; the ink reads "K LABEL", the -1
! revision's own flowchart box prints "KLABEL", and its typeset
! symbol index lists KLABEL (alphabetically between KKSPAC and
! KLOCAT).  So the prose is the odd one out and the ink stands.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE SPAN, ESTABLISHED FROM THE PAGE (no survey endpoint quoted)
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   FIRST located row   line  4   221370.00   (a printed "SLC,$")
!   FIRST emitting row  line  8   221370.00
!   LAST  row           line 47   221415.00
!   printed lines       47        (line column, 1..47, continuous)
!   cards               40        (LG000001..LG000040, continuous)
!   located rows        40
!
! NOTHING FELL OFF EITHER END.  The line column runs 1..47 with no
! break; line 47 is followed by blank paper, not by a cut.  The card
! column's own header, "CARD ID LG000001", agrees with line 1.
!
! THE CARD COUNT IS 40 AND THE ROW COUNT IS 47 BECAUSE SEVEN CARDS
! PRINT TWO LINES EACH -- two statements punched on one card:
!
!   lines 22/23  LG000022   SIC,K K RET    ; B,K IO REJ
!   lines 24/25  LG000023   LVI,1,$+1.0    ; B,J SEOP T
!   lines 30/31  LG000028   CB,2,K REPET.32; B,K SOS
!   lines 33/34  LG000030   SIC,J BSP X    ; B,J BSP E
!   lines 37/38  LG000033   LVE,9,R V4     ; SV,9,R RDL
!   lines 39/40  LG000034   SIC,K K RET    ; B,K IO REJ
!   lines 41/42  LG000035   LVI,1,$+1.0    ; B,J SEOP T
!
! Five of the seven are the SIC-pair or branch-pair shape p.184
! already recorded; LVE;SV and LVI;B are not, so the rule really is
! "one card, one WORD", not "one card, one SIC pair".
!
! >>> THE SEPARATOR GLYPH, RENDERED AT 1600 dpi, IS A VERTICAL BAR
! >>> WITH TWO CROSSBARS -- a double-dagger shape, not a semicolon.
! It appears in line 6's comment ("SIC,K K IND<sep>B,K IO IND") and
! the volume OCR of printed pp.190 and 191 shows the same glyph in
! the same place in two more calling-sequence comments.  It is only
! ever inside a COMMENT card here, so nothing in this deck depends
! on naming it; I record the shape and do not claim a character.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> WHAT THIS PAGE'S ORIGIN SAYS ABOUT pp.185-187 -- 71 WORDS <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! An SLC emits nothing, so the LOCATION this page prints beside its
! "SLC,$" is the counter ARRIVING from the page before.  That is a
! constraint on the three pages being transcribed beside this one,
! and it is worth stating because no one of them can see it:
!
!   printed p.184's last word (its "R RDL XW,$,1.0,$")  0o221260
!   printed p.188's first word (this page's SLC)        0o221370
!   therefore pp.185, 186 and 187 TOGETHER own exactly
!       0o221261 .. 0o221367  =  71 WORDS, with no hole
!
! If the three of them do not close on 71 words, a row has fallen
! off one of them, or one of them has a DR/DRZ or a forward SLC that
! must be named.  This deck cannot say which; it can say the total.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE ORIGIN IS CHECKED, NOT ASSERTED, AND BY THREE PAGES. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The page prints "SLC,$" (line 4), so this deck must substitute a
! hard "SLC, (8)221370.0" and the arriving counter cannot contradict
! it (workflow, WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE item 2).  But the merge
! can, and it does: THREE INDEPENDENT WITNESSES already placed the
! two labels this page defines at its first two words.
!
!   * printed p.155's landed deck SYNs KIOIND at (8)221370.0 and
!     KKIND at (8)221371.0 -- both already in the body image before
!     this page existed.
!   * printed p.156's landed deck SYNs EINDR and KKIND at
!     (8)221371.0 off three SICs, which pin the word to the BIT.
!   * the volume OCR carries FIVE pages, all of them already landed,
!     whose "SIC,K K IND" (or its "SIC,E IND R" alias) compiles
!     221371.00 and whose "B,K IO IND" compiles 221370.10 --
!     MEASURED, printed pp.155, 156, 160, 163 and 183, ten rows
!     between them.
!
! MEASURED INJECTION, as the brief asks: move this deck's SLC one
! half word to (8)221370.40 and re-merge the body image.  It is
! REFUSED --
!     FAIL KIOIND: printed p.155 SYNs bit 4767232,
!                  printed p.188 places it at bit 4767264
! -- so the origin of this page is CHECKED.  (The run is recorded
! under WHAT I COULD NOT SETTLE only in the sense that it says
! nothing about the BIT within the half word; the SICs from p.156
! say that.)
!
! AND A FOURTH WITNESS, FOR A LABEL IN THE MIDDLE OF THE PAGE: the
! volume OCR's printed p.189 line 6 is "221420.00  221406.50 00
! B,K R NEW  -NEW TAPE IS READY", and 221406.50 is K R NEW's half
! word plus the branch's own .10.  K R NEW is this page's line 35 at
! 221406.40.  A page nobody has transcribed yet agrees with this
! deck's counter twenty-eight rows in.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE TWO EXTERNALS THE CALLER ASKED ABOUT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THIS PAGE DEFINES NEITHER "JCNAD" NOR "YFXAD". <<<  Neither
! name, and neither address (0o215006, 0o216440), appears anywhere
! in the forty-seven lines; this page's whole range is 221370-221415
! and every one of its seven labels is listed under !SYM below.
! Looked for explicitly, not noticed to be absent.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPH CALLS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) "K SOS" (lines 26, 28, 31, 43).  The second character is the
!     usual round glyph and shape cannot settle it.  It did not have
!     to: printed p.125's landed deck already SYNs KSOS at
!     (8)221274.0, which is the address all four of these rows
!     compile.  Spelling taken from the landed deck, address from
!     this page.
!
! (2) "KVI" (lines 11, 13, 15, 17) is NOT a misread LVI.  The K and
!     the L are different glyphs here -- lines 24 and 41 print a
!     clean "LVI" on the same page -- and the BYTES part them
!     outright: KVI compiles 04 and LVI compiles 01.  KVI is in
!     C22-6531's value-operation family (strap_asm's IMM_INDEX_CODES)
!     and assembles; the page's own bytes are the confirmation.
!
! (3) "J SEOP T" (lines 25, 42) HAS A J, AND IT IS NOT "KSEOPT".
!     This one is worth the space because the typeset manual votes
!     the other way and is right about a DIFFERENT symbol.  C22-6728's
!     symbol index lists KSEOPT and no JSEOPT, and the landed decks
!     for printed pp.152, 154, 159, 164 and 165 all SYN KSEOPT at
!     (8)221350.40.  This page's rows compile 221525.10.  Those are
!     two different addresses, so they are two different symbols --
!     and the volume OCR's printed p.192 line 27 is the DEFINING
!     card, "221525.00  000036.35 02  J SEOP T  LCI,14,K REP", with
!     the same banner above it naming the linkage "B,JSEOPT".
!     At 1600 dpi the glyph is the hooked vertical of line 33's
!     "J BSP X", not the two diagonals of line 11's "KVI".
!
! (4) "LX,0,S IO INS($12)" (lines 20, 35).  The index field prints a
!     round glyph.  An index field can only hold a number, so it is
!     a 0 -- the octal-field argument, rung 5.  Corroborated by the
!     byte: .00 1C is what J=0 produces.
!
! (5) "CM1111(BU,1),$0.52" (lines 21, 36).  THE SAME STATEMENT TWICE
!     ON ONE PAGE -- rung 4, the strongest rung.  Line 21 prints its
!     last byte as a clean closed F0 and line 36 prints it open; they
!     are one statement and the byte is F0.  printed p.18 prints
!     "CM1111(BU,1)" six times and every one is 001000.36 F0.
!     "$0" is INDEX REGISTER 0, whose cell is word 0o20, which is why
!     the first half word prints 000020.64 and not 000000.64; .52 is
!     a bare decimal bit offset and 52 decimal is 0o64.  Both facts
!     are checked by the compiled word, not asserted.
!
! (6) "R RDL" (line 38) has a D.  printed p.184's line 36 is the
!     DEFINING card, "R RDL  XW,$,1.0,$" at 221260.00, and this row's
!     221260.23 is that word.
!
! (7) "B0" on line 10 (printed "BO" to the eye).  Settled on what
!     produced it: LVE,2 against K K IND, which this deck compiles,
!     and the hex byte of an LVE has no low-nibble index term here.
!
! (8) THE LINE-NUMBER ASTERISK IS NOT A MARKER AND IS NOT THIS
!     PAGE'S.  Every one of the forty-seven lines prints "N*"
!     immediately after its line number.  I checked printed p.184
!     at the identical crop geometry and IT DOES TOO, on lines 1 and
!     11 which that deck records as unmarked.  So the asterisk the
!     workflow calls "the location-column asterisk" is the SECOND
!     one, printed after the LOCATION field, and on this page
!     exactly ONE row carries it: LINE 28, "221403.00 *", whose
!     statement is "B,K SOS" and whose comment is "-EE - IMPOSSIBLE".
!     Lines 26 and 31 are the SAME statement compiling the SAME word
!     and are NOT marked, which kills the obvious guess.
!     I propose no rule from one page (the brief forbids it); I name
!     the page that would kill the nearest hypothesis below.
!
! (9) >>> LINE 37's BYTE IS B0 AND I FIRST READ IT 80. <<<  Worth
!     the space because of how it was caught and how it was settled.
!     At 900 dpi the glyph is two stacked bowls and reads 8; the
!     oracle refused the row, which is the whole argument for handing
!     the assembler the printed form and letting a row fail.  Settled
!     by rendering it beside line 36's CERTAIN 8 (the first half of a
!     CM1111 full word, which line 21 prints identically and which
!     printed p.18 prints six times) at 1600 dpi, cropped from one
!     render so the two are at the same scale:
!       line 36   both bowls closed, rounded left side      -> 8
!       line 37   a STRAIGHT VERTICAL LEFT STEM the full
!                 height, flat top-left corner, bowls open
!                 to the right                              -> B
!     That is the workflow's own B/8 discriminator -- the stroke a
!     worn drum loses first -- used in the direction it is safe in:
!     dropout thins a stem, it never grows one.  Line 10 is the same
!     mnemonic (LVE) on the same page and prints a clean B0, so the
!     page itself carries the control.
!     WHAT THIS ROW IS NOT: it is not evidence about the J field.
!     LVE's byte is B0 for every J (measured over all 32 index
!     mnemonics against this operand: nothing in the set prints 80
!     with a .23 address, which is what first said the reading was
!     wrong rather than the statement).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT I COULD NOT SETTLE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (A) THE BIT OFFSET OF ELEVEN EXTERNALS.  Only three rows on this
!     page read their operand to the bit: the three SICs (lines 22,
!     33, 39), which pin K K RET to 221512.40 and J BSP X to
!     221520.40 exactly.  There is no VFL row with a symbolic
!     operand on this page -- line 21's CM1111 addresses an index
!     register, not a symbol -- so for every B, BXE, KVI, LVE, SV
!     and CB target only BIT 32 is observable.  The ".00"/".40" in
!     each SYN below is therefore a reading of the HALF WORD and a
!     CONVENTION below it.  Where another page's defining card is
!     known, that card is cited and the bit comes from there.
!
! (B) THE SEPARATOR GLYPH ON LINE 6 (see above).  I can describe its
!     shape and I cannot name the character.  C22-6531 and C28-6129
!     were grepped for "semicolon" and for any statement-separator
!     prose and neither says anything; the character does not occur
!     outside comment cards in this corpus as far as I can see.  It
!     costs nothing here and it will cost the person who one day
!     wants to reproduce a two-statement card.
!
! (C) WHY LINE 28 CARRIES THE LOCATION ASTERISK.  Eight things it is
!     not are already recorded elsewhere; here is a ninth, measured
!     on this page: it is NOT "the row is a duplicate of an earlier
!     row", because lines 26 and 31 duplicate it exactly and are
!     clean.  HYPOTHESIS, offered as a hypothesis: it marks the
!     SECOND half word of a card whose FIRST half word printed on
!     the previous line -- line 28 is LG000026 and line 27 is
!     LG000025, so that is already false on this page.  I could not
!     construct a surviving rule.  THE PAGE THAT WOULD KILL ANY RULE
!     I COULD PROPOSE IS printed p.189, whose volume OCR shows at
!     least one asterisked row (line 32 at 221510.00) in a context
!     unlike this one.
!
! (D) THE BLANKS INSIDE NAMES.  The page prints "K IO IND",
!     "R V4", "K K SPAC" with blanks and "RV4"/"KREPET" closed up in
!     places; strap_asm strips blanks from a name, so the deck cannot
!     tell the two apart and neither can any check here.  Line 15
!     prints "R V4" with a clear gap and line 37 prints "RV4" closed,
!     in the same operand position, which is at least evidence the
!     blanks are compositor's spacing and not part of the name.
!
! (E) >>> "K COUNT" AND "K R UK" REST ON INK ALONE, PERMANENTLY. <<<
!     Of the seven labels this page defines, five are checked from
!     outside it: K IO IND and K K IND by five landed pages' SYNs
!     and SICs, K R NEW by printed p.189's branch to it, and
!     K R READ and K REPET by printed p.189's "K R EE
!     CB,2,K R READ.32" and by C22-6728's own list of this routine's
!     five paths.  K COUNT and K RUK are in NEITHER -- they were
!     absent from the body image before this deck and the typeset
!     symbol index of C22-6728-1 runs KQIN, KREPET, KRETRY, KRIO,
!     KRITET, KRNEW, KRREAD, KRWEF, KSEOPT with NO KCOUNT and NO
!     KRUK between them.  So once this page lands they are defined
!     and unreferenced: the merge can never fail on them and the
!     oracle is blind to spellings.  Their only witnesses are rung 1
!     -- "COUNT" is an English word and line 44's own comment is
!     "-UK" beside "B,K R UK".  That is probably right and it is
!     exactly the class of error that has bitten this corpus before
!     (T FMCDE, K OBJ R).  A later page that BRANCHES to either one
!     would settle it; printed p.189 or p.190 is where to look.
!
! (F) THE SEPARATOR GLYPH, continued.  strap/charsets.py was checked:
!     the 7030's A set (the alphanumeric one) has NO semicolon at all
!     and its IQS set has one, at code 0o012, which is "0" in A.
!     That is a LEAD and not an answer -- it would explain a card
!     punched with a separator printing as something the A chain does
!     not have a glyph for -- and I did not pursue it, because the
!     glyph only ever occurs in comment cards here.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> FALSIFIABLE PREDICTIONS FOR printed p.189 (PDF p.196) <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   (1) ITS FIRST LOCATED ROW IS 221415.40.  This page ends at
!       221415.00 with a half word, so the counter arrives there;
!       and the volume OCR's first row on PDF p.196 is
!       "221415.40  000011.77 80  221274.34 00  BZB,$R.63,K SOS
!        -IF UK ALONE, MACHINE ERROR", which is the continuation of
!       this page's K R UK.  If p.189's line 1 is not 221415.40, one
!       of us is wrong.
!   (2) ITS FIRST CARD SERIAL IS LG000041.  WEAKER than (1): the
!       brief records two measured serials that print no listing
!       line, both at page breaks.  A serial BELOW LG000041 would
!       falsify the join; a missing LG000041 would not.
!   (3) ITS HEADING-ROW LOCATION FIELD READS 221415, because the
!       volume OCR's PDF p.196 line 1 is a located row, not a
!       banner.  (Contrast this page, whose line 1 is a banner and
!       whose field is blank.)
!   (4) p.189 DEFINES K R EE (221420.40), K R NEW is NOT redefined
!       there -- this page owns it -- and p.189 also defines
!       K LABEL (221421.40), K K EXIT (221422.40) and K K SPAC
!       (221424.00).  All four are SYNned below, so if p.189's
!       defining cards disagree the merge will say so.  K R WEF
!       (221444.40) belongs to printed p.190, not p.189: the OCR's
!       page break falls between p.189's last row at 221444.00 and
!       that defining card.
!   (5) p.189 line 6 is "B,K R NEW" at 221420.00 compiling
!       221406.50.  That is this deck's line 35 seen from outside.
!   (6) p.189 carries "E IND R SYN(BU,40,10),K K IND" at 221371.00+
!       -- an ALIAS of this page's line 9 label WITH A DATA
!       DESCRIPTION.  p.156's landed deck already SYNs EINDR with
!       NO dds.  Whoever transcribes p.189 should write the printed
!       (BU,40,10) and expect the merge to have an opinion about
!       p.156; that is a real disagreement between two landed
!       pages and this deck cannot settle it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE NAME FIELD AND THE BLANK -- TWO ASSEMBLER REFUSALS, MEASURED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The printed form was handed to strap_asm FIRST, as rule 2 says, and
! TWO SHAPES OF PRINTED CARD WERE REFUSED.  Both are the known gaps
! the brief lists; both are recorded here with what they printed.
!
! (i) A BLANK IN THE NAME (LABEL) FIELD.  The page prints seven
!     labels with blanks -- "K IO IND", "K K IND", "K REPET",
!     "K COUNT", "K R READ", "K R NEW", "K R UK".  Handed over as
!     printed, the first one gives
!         line 321: unknown mnemonic 'KINDBRZ'
!     -- the parser takes the first blank as the end of the name and
!     the rest of the card as the operation.  So every label in this
!     deck is written CLOSED UP and its printed spelling is in the
!     comment on its own line.  This is the house convention already
!     (printed p.184 writes KRELOD and KBOUNC the same way); it is
!     recorded because the deck must not look as though the page
!     printed it that way.
!
! (ii) A BLANK IN A NAME INSIDE AN EXPRESSION.  Lines 30 and 47
!     print "CB,2,K REPET.32" and "CB,2,K R READ.32".  MEASURED,
!     against SYNs of both names:
!         CB,2,K REPET.32    -> undefined symbol 'K'
!         CB,2,K R READ.32   -> undefined symbol 'K'
!     and the bare names resolve perfectly in every other row of
!     this deck ("B,K SOS", "BXE,K R READ", "KVI,2,K FIL K1" all
!     carry blanks and all assemble).  THE BRIEF'S EXAMPLES OF THIS
!     GAP BOTH HAVE AN OPERATOR ("S TLR+14.", "K GOOF+.32"); these
!     two have only the dotted bit offset, so the gap is wider than
!     the examples and this page measures it.  Lines 30 and 47 are
!     written "CB,2,KREPET.32" and "CB,2,KRREAD.32", flagged at both
!     occurrences.  Nothing else about those rows changes -- their
!     !CHECKs are the printed bytes and they pass.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! JOINING THIS PAGE TO THE STANDING BODY-IMAGE TEST
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! tests/check_mcp_body_image.py carries "FIRST, LAST = 99, 184" and
! asserts body_page_count == 85.  This deck was merged by hand-
! appending itself to that list and the merge is clean (773 defined,
! 75 external, ZERO unaccounted words).  THE TEST ITSELF CANNOT BE
! EDITED YET: the range is contiguous, so it cannot reach 188 until
! 185, 186 and 187 land.  When they do, the edit is
!     FIRST, LAST = 99, 188     and     body_page_count == 89
! (85 + four pages, assuming none of 185-187 is a compiles-nothing
! page needing an entry in strap/mcp_image.py's NO_DECK_PAGES; each
! such page subtracts one).  NOT strap/mcp_image.py's MCP_IPL_PAGES
! -- pp.15-98 and pp.99+ are two assemblies.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every one is a stand-in SYN, never a copy of a defining card.
! "landed" = already in the merged body image; "OCR" = read off the
! volume OCR of a DIFFERENT printed page, which is a finding aid for
! WHERE a symbol is defined and is cited as such.

SIOIND  SYN(BU,5), 1.09              ! landed p.102 line 7 -IO INDICATORS; line 8 prints 000001.11
SIOINS  SYN(BU,64), 4.0              ! landed p.101 line 17 -IO INSTR. LAST; lines 20/35 print 000004.00
KREP    SYN(BU,18), 30               ! A COUNT, not an address; lines 19/32 print 000036 = 0o36 = 30.  THE dds IS CARRIED, NOT INVENTED: printed p.185 line 27 PRINTS the defining card "K REP SYN(BU,18),30" and printed p.125's landed deck records it.  Written without it, the merge REFUSES -- "KREP is declared with more than one data description: (no dds) on printed p.188; (BU,18) on printed p.125" -- which is the body image doing its job and is recorded here because this deck's first draft hit it
KSOS    SYN, (8)221274.0             ! landed p.125; lines 26/28/31/43 print 221274.10 -- half word only
KFILK1  SYN, (8)220171.40            ! landed p.163 defines it; line 11 prints 220171.45 -- half word only
KKFDEN  SYN, (8)217746.40            ! landed p.156 defines it; line 13 prints 217746.45 -- half word only
KWLTMK  SYN, (8)217757.40            ! landed p.156 defines it; line 17 prints 217757.45 -- half word only
RV4     SYN, (8)221201.00            ! landed p.183 defines it; lines 15/37 print 221201.05 / .23
RRDL    SYN, (8)221260.00            ! landed p.184 line 36 "R RDL XW,$,1.0,$"; line 38 prints 221260.23
KKSPAC  SYN, (8)221424.00            ! OCR printed p.189 "221424.00 K K SPAC LCI,2,K REP"; line 12 prints 221424.32
KLABEL  SYN, (8)221421.40            ! OCR printed p.189 "221421.40 221660.00 80 K LABEL SIC,JWRITX"; line 14 prints 221421.72
KRWEF   SYN, (8)221444.40            ! OCR printed p.190 line 1 "221444.40 000036.05 02 K R WEF LCI,2,K REP"; line 18 prints 221444.72
KKEXIT  SYN, (8)221422.40            ! OCR printed p.189 line 10's defining card; lines 29/46 print 221422.50
KREE    SYN, (8)221420.40            ! OCR printed p.189 "221420.40 221405.44 48 K R EE CB,2,K R READ.32"; line 45 prints 221420.50
