! EVERY ONE OF THE FORTY LOCATED ROWS CARRIES A !CHECK BELOW.  No
! row on this page is unchecked and no word in 221370..221415 is
! unaccounted for.

!SYM KIOIND 221370.00
!SYM KKIND  221371.00
!SYM KREPET 221376.00
!SYM KCOUNT 221404.00
!SYM KRREAD 221405.00
!SYM KRNEW  221406.40
!SYM KRUK   221415.00
!
!CHECK 221370.00 | 000001.11 8D 002000.20 50 | line 8 K IO IND L(BU,2),S IO IND($13) -TEST IF EPGK OR UK ON -- S IO IND is p.102's SYN(BU,5),1.09 and 1.09 DECIMAL is word 1 bit 9 = 0o11, so the bit-address conversion is checked outright; 8D's low nibble is index $13; the second word is the (BU,2) dds (0o002000) with the L code 20 50
!CHECK 221371.00 | 221371.34 C2 | line 9 K K IND BRZ,$ -IF NONE ON, ALLS WELL -- $ is this row, so the address half is a tautology, but 0o34 is the RZ indicator with bit 32 CLEAR and that is a real reading of the branch. Eight other pages' "SIC,K K IND" compile 221371.00 against this label
!CHECK 221371.40 | 221371.05 B0 | line 10 LVE,2,K K IND -- the SAME label as line 9 through a different operation: .05 for J=2 with bit 32 clear. The byte prints "BO" and is B0; an LVE has no index term in its low nibble here
!CHECK 221372.00 | 220171.45 04 | line 11 KVI,2,K FIL K1 -TEST IF SPACE FILE OP -- K FIL K1 is printed p.163's defining card at 220171.40; 0o45 is 0o40 OR 5, so bit 32 IS SET and the landed .40 is confirmed. The byte 04 is KVI's, against LVI's 01 on line 24 -- the two mnemonics are parted by the page's own bytes
!CHECK 221372.40 | 221424.32 C2 | line 12 BXE,K K SPAC -- 0o32 is the XE indicator with bit 32 CLEAR, so K K SPAC is at 221424.00; the volume OCR's printed p.189 prints its defining card there, "221424.00 K K SPAC LCI,2,K REP". C22-6728 lists KKSPAC as path 1 of this routine
!CHECK 221373.00 | 217746.45 04 | line 13 KVI,2,K KF DEN -TEST IF W LABEL OP -- K KF DEN is printed p.156's defining card at 217746.40; 0o45 confirms bit 32
!CHECK 221373.40 | 221421.72 C2 | line 14 BXE,K LABEL -- 0o72 is 0o40 OR the XE indicator 0o32, so K LABEL is at 221421.40, which is where the volume OCR's printed p.189 prints "K LABEL SIC,JWRITX". The prose of C22-6728 calls this path "KLABWL"; its flowchart and its symbol index both print KLABEL and the ink agrees with them
!CHECK 221374.00 | 221201.05 04 | line 15 KVI,2,R V4 -TEST IF RD LABEL OP -- R V4 is printed p.183's label at 221201.00 and 0o05 has bit 32 CLEAR, which confirms it. Line 37 reaches the same symbol through an LVE and prints 221201.23, so the two rows are each other's control
!CHECK 221374.40 | 221405.32 C2 | line 16 BXE,K R READ -- K R READ is THIS page's line 32 at 221405.00, so this is a real address check and not a tautology: 0o32 is XE with bit 32 clear. C22-6728 lists KRREAD as path 3
!CHECK 221375.00 | 217757.45 04 | line 17 KVI,2,K WL TMK -TEST IF WEF OP -- K WL TMK is printed p.156's defining card at 217757.40; 0o45 confirms bit 32
!CHECK 221375.40 | 221444.72 C2 | line 18 BXE,K R WEF -- 0o72 is 0o40 OR XE, so K R WEF is at 221444.40, where the volume OCR's printed p.190 prints its defining card -- the PAGE BREAK falls between p.189's last row at 221444.00 and that card. C22-6728 lists KRWEF as path 4
!CHECK 221376.00 | 000036.05 02 | line 19 K REPET LCI,2,K REP -OTHERWISE, LOC OR DENSITY OP -- K REP is a COUNT, not an address: printed p.125 SYNs it 30 and 30 decimal is 0o36, which is the whole address field. .05 is J=2. C22-6728 lists KREPET as path 5
!CHECK 221376.40 | 000004.00 1C | line 20 LX,0,S IO INS($12) -- S IO INS is p.101's SYN(BU,64),4.0 at word 4; .00 is J=0, which is what settles the round glyph in the index field (an index field can only hold a number)
!CHECK 221377.00 | 000020.64 80 001000.36 F0 | line 21 CM1111(BU,1),$0.52 -MAKE IT SEOP COMMAND -- "$0" is INDEX REGISTER 0, whose cell is word 0o20, so the address prints 000020 and not 000000; ".52" is a bare DECIMAL bit offset and 52 decimal is 0o64. The second word is the (BU,1) dds with the CM1111 code 36 F0, which printed p.18 prints six times. Line 36 is the same card and prints the same word, which is how the open round glyph in line 36's byte is settled
!CHECK 221400.00 | 221512.40 80 | line 22 SIC,K K RET -- A SIC CARRIES ITS OPERAND'S FULL 24-BIT ADDRESS, so this row READS K K RET at 221512.40 TO THE BIT. The volume OCR's printed p.191 line 37 prints the defining card there, "221512.40 221512.44 44 K K RET BZCBJZ,$ -RETURN". Line 39 is the same card and its control
!CHECK 221400.40 | 221505.10 00 | line 23 B,K IO REJ -AND RETRY -- target+.10, so only bit 32 is checked: K IO REJ at 221505.00, which the volume OCR's printed p.191 line 21 prints as the defining card "221505.00 000036.03 02 K IO REJ LCI,1,K REP". This card is the same card as line 22, and p.191's own banner prints the pair as a calling sequence
!CHECK 221401.00 | 221402.03 01 | line 24 LVI,1,$+1.0 -- $ is 221401.00 so $+1.0 is 221402.00 and .03 is 2J+1 = 3 for J=1 with bit 32 clear. The byte 01 is LVI's against the 04 of lines 11/13/15/17's KVI, which is the eliminator for that glyph
!CHECK 221401.40 | 221525.10 00 | line 25 B,J SEOP T -CHECK TERMINATION -- J SEOP T at 221525.00. THIS IS NOT KSEOPT, which five landed decks place at 221350.40; the volume OCR's printed p.192 line 27 is the defining card, "221525.00 000036.35 02 J SEOP T LCI,14,K REP"
!CHECK 221402.00 | 221274.10 00 | line 26 B,K SOS -EPGK - GIVE UP -- K SOS at 221274.00, landed by printed p.125's deck, which is also where the spelling of the round glyph comes from
!CHECK 221402.40 | 221404.10 00 | line 27 B,K COUNT -UK -- K COUNT is THIS page's line 30 at 221404.00, so the 0o10 is a real reading of bit 32 against a label the page itself places
!CHECK 221403.00 | 221274.10 00 | line 28 B,K SOS -EE - IMPOSSIBLE -- the same word as lines 26 and 31. THIS ROW CARRIES THE PAGE'S ONLY LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK and lines 26 and 31 do not, which is the measurement that kills "the asterisk marks a repeated word"
!CHECK 221403.40 | 221422.50 00 | line 29 B,K K EXIT -SUCCESSFUL END -- 0o40 OR 0o10 = 0o50, so K K EXIT is at 221422.40, where the volume OCR's printed p.189 line 10 prints its defining card. Line 46 is the same statement and prints the same word
!CHECK 221404.00 | 221376.44 48 | line 30 K COUNT CB,2,K REPET.32 -- >>> THIS ROW CHECKS THE BARE-DECIMAL OFFSET RULE ON THIS PAGE'S OWN LABELS. <<< K REPET is line 19 at 221376.00; ".32" is BARE DECIMAL, so 32 decimal is 0o40 and the target is 221376.40; 0o44 is that 0o40 OR the CB's own 0o04. Line 47 does the identical arithmetic against K R READ and prints 221405.44, so the rule is checked twice on one page against two labels
!CHECK 221404.40 | 221274.10 00 | line 31 B,K SOS -TRY KREP TIMES BEFORE GIVING UP -- same card as line 30; the third of four identical words, and unmarked
!CHECK 221405.00 | 000036.05 02 | line 32 K R READ LCI,2,K REP -- the same count and the same J as line 19, at a different address, so the two rows are each other's control on the 0o36
!CHECK 221405.40 | 221520.40 80 | line 33 SIC,J BSP X -- SIC, so J BSP X is read at 221520.40 BIT-EXACT. The volume OCR's printed p.192 line 8 prints "221520.40 221520.50 00 JBSPX B,$", its own defining card at exactly that address
!CHECK 221406.00 | 221514.10 00 | line 34 B,J BSP E -BACKSPACE TO LOAD POINT -- same card as line 33; J BSP E at 221514.00. The volume OCR's printed p.191 line 42 opens the BACKSPACE ROUTINE with the banner "LINKAGE SIC,JBSPX / B,JBSPE", which is this card named from outside, and C22-6728 lists JBSPE among the short subroutines of this very routine
!CHECK 221406.40 | 000004.00 1C | line 35 K R NEW LX,0,S IO INS($12) -- the same word as line 20 under a label. >>> THE LABEL IS CHECKED FROM OUTSIDE: the volume OCR's printed p.189 line 6 is "221420.00 221406.50 00 B,K R NEW -NEW TAPE IS READY", and 221406.50 is this label's half word plus the branch's 0o10
!CHECK 221407.00 | 000020.64 80 001000.36 F0 | line 36 CM1111(BU,1),$0.52 -MAKE IT SEOP COMMAND -- the same statement as line 21. Its printed byte is open where line 21's is closed; one statement, one page, one drum, same character position -- the strongest rung of the glyph ladder, and it says F0
!CHECK 221410.00 | 221201.23 B0 | line 37 LVE,9,RV4 -- R V4 again, now with J=9: 0o23 is 2J+1 = 19 with bit 32 clear, against line 15's 0o05 for J=2. Two operations, two index registers, one symbol, and the pair pins the half word. THE BYTE IS B0 AND MY FIRST READING WAS 80 -- see GLYPH CALL (9)
!CHECK 221410.40 | 221260.23 30 | line 38 SV,9,R RDL -- same card as line 37; R RDL is printed p.184's line 36 index word at 221260.00, and the same 0o23 as line 37 confirms J=9. The D of RDL is p.184's, not this page's ink
!CHECK 221411.00 | 221512.40 80 | line 39 SIC,K K RET -- the same SIC as line 22, so K K RET's 221512.40 is read twice on this page to the bit
!CHECK 221411.40 | 221505.10 00 | line 40 B,K IO REJ -AND RETRY -- same card as line 39; the same word as line 23
!CHECK 221412.00 | 221413.03 01 | line 41 LVI,1,$+1.0 -- the same statement as line 24 at a different $, so the row checks the location counter as well as the operation: $ is 221412.00 and $+1.0 is 221413.00
!CHECK 221412.40 | 221525.10 00 | line 42 B,J SEOP T -CHECK TERMINATION -- same card as line 41; the same word as line 25
!CHECK 221413.00 | 221274.10 00 | line 43 B,K SOS -EPGK - GIVE UP -- the fourth and last of the identical K SOS branches
!CHECK 221413.40 | 221415.10 00 | line 44 B,K R UK -UK -- K R UK is THIS page's line 47 at 221415.00, the last row on the page, so this row is a forward reference the page closes itself
!CHECK 221414.00 | 221420.50 00 | line 45 B,K R EE -EE -- 0o40 OR 0o10, so K R EE is at 221420.40, where the volume OCR's printed p.189 line 8 prints the defining card "221420.40 221405.44 48 K R EE CB,2,K R READ.32" -- which is also, word for word, this page's line 47 with the same operand
!CHECK 221414.40 | 221422.50 00 | line 46 B,K K EXIT -SUCCESSFUL END -- the same word as line 29
!CHECK 221415.00 | 221405.44 48 | line 47 K R UK CB,2,K R READ.32 -TRY KREP TIMES BEFORE GIVING UP -- K R READ is line 32 at 221405.00 and ".32" bare decimal is 0o40, so the target is 221405.40 and 0o44 is 0o40 OR the CB's 0o04. THE LAST ROW ON THE PAGE; the counter leaves at 221415.40, which is what printed p.189's line 1 should print
